From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:27:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] meta-ibm: p10bmc: enable OTP image generation

The otptool class creates OTP images whenever SOCSEC_SIGN_ENABLE is
set. The next change gives it its own switch, OTP_IMAGE_ENABLE, so
that SoCs that don't sign with socsec can create them too.

p10bmc sets OTPTOOL_CONFIGS for its U-Boot, and socsec-sign verifies
the signed SPL against the OTP images, so set OTP_IMAGE_ENABLE ahead of
that change. pstbmc includes p10bmc.conf and gets it too. Nothing reads
the variable yet.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
---
 meta-ibm/conf/machine/p10bmc.conf | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/meta-ibm/conf/machine/p10bmc.conf b/meta-ibm/conf/machine/p10bmc.conf
index aaee528..0a894bf 100644
--- a/meta-ibm/conf/machine/p10bmc.conf
+++ b/meta-ibm/conf/machine/p10bmc.conf
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ UBOOT_SIGN_KEYDIR = "${UNPACKDIR}"
 SPL_SIGN_KEYDIR = "${UNPACKDIR}"
 
 SOCSEC_SIGN_ENABLE = "1"
+OTP_IMAGE_ENABLE = "1"
 
 DEBUG_TRIGGERS = "kcs2"
 PACKAGECONFIG:append:pn-debug-trigger = " triggers"
